+# Generator self-check: multi-turn Q&A conversation history
+
+This is the Generator's own evidence. It is **not** the Evaluator's `verification-report.md`: the Evaluator should still run §6 of `sprint-contract.md` independently.
+
+- **Date:** 2026-11-15
+- **Commits:**
+  - `b17561e`: Step 0 baseline type fix
+  - `96007e7`: preload sandbox fix (see deviation D-1 below)
+  - the feature commit that follows them
+
+## Contract deviations
+
+`sprint-contract.md` was left unedited, as the user instructed, so deviations are recorded here instead of in its "Contract deviations" section.
+
+### D-1: preload fix outside the feature scope (commit `96007e7`)
+
+- **What:** `src/preload/preload.ts` no longer `require`s `../shared/types` at runtime. It keeps a local channel map typed as `typeof IPC_CHANNELS` through a type-only import, so the compiler still rejects any drift from `src/shared/types.ts`. Checked: changing `'qa:ask'` to `'qa:askx'` fails `tsc` with TS2322.
+- **Why:** with Electron 33, preloads are sandboxed by default and can only require `electron`. The original preload threw `module not found: ../shared/types` ("Unable to load preload script" in the renderer console), so `window.knowledgeBase` was `undefined`. No IPC worked, §6.2 seeding was impossible, and AC-1–AC-13 could not be verified at all. The contract's §2 did not catch this because `npm run build` succeeds and the failure only appears at runtime.
+- **Impact on criteria:** none. There is no new IPC channel, no service or main-process change, and no change to the `qa-history.json` schema. It is a narrow supporting fix, as `AGENTS.md` allows ("unless a blocker forces a narrow supporting fix"). §5 asks for the IPC layer to stay unchanged unless a criterion cannot be met otherwise, and here none of them could be.
+
+## How this was verified
+
+The built app (`npx tsc -p tsconfig.node.json && vite build`, the same build steps as `npm run dev`) was launched as:
+
+```
+env -u NODE_OPTIONS npx electron . --user-data-dir=<scratch>/ud --remote-debugging-port=9333
+```
+
+- **Isolated data dir.** `--user-data-dir` points at a scratch directory, so the real `~/Library/Application Support/knowledge-base` was never touched.
+- **`NODE_OPTIONS`.** On this machine `NODE_OPTIONS` contains `--openssl-legacy-provider`, which Electron rejects, so it has to be unset.
+- **How the app was driven.** `scripts/phase1.mjs` and `scripts/phase2.mjs` drive the app through the Chrome DevTools Protocol (zero dependencies; Node 20 with `--experimental-websocket`). They use real `Input.dispatchKeyEvent`/`dispatchMouseEvent` events (Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, clicks), take screenshots with `Page.captureScreenshot`, and listen for `Runtime.exceptionThrown` and `console.error`.
+- **Restarts.** A restart is SIGTERM to Electron followed by a relaunch with the same data dir. That is equivalent to Cmd+Q, because the app has no unsaved state and `qa-history.json` is written synchronously on every ask.
+- **Fixture.** The §6.3 fixture script was run verbatim between quit and relaunch.
+
+Raw results are in `phase1-results.json`, `phase2-restart-results.json` and `phase2-after-clear-results.json`. Logs are in `run1.log` (session 1), `run2.log` (restart and clear) and `run3.log` (restart after clear).
+
