+| AC-13 | PASS | `div[role=log][aria-live=polite]` > `ol` > `li` > `article[aria-label="Exchange n of N"]`. The input is named by `<label for=question-input>`. Citations are `<button>`s and there are no clickable divs. Keyboard-only path: focus the input, type, Enter, Shift+Tab to the newest citation (`:focus-visible` outline `#8888bb`, `08`), Enter opens the document |
+| AC-14 | PASS | Renderer uses only `window.knowledgeBase`. A single `interface Window` in `src/renderer/types.d.ts` (the duplicate in `App.tsx` was removed). No service, main or IPC changes |
+| AC-15 | PASS | `ConversationHistory.tsx` deleted (the TODO is gone); `lastResponse` removed; `npm run build` passes |
+
+**Log checks (§6.8), `run1.log`:**
+
+- 6 initialization lines at startup
+- 10 `ASK_QUESTION` lines = 9 `Q&A response` + 1 `Q&A failed`
+- the `citationCount` values `2,2,0,2,2,2,2,2,2` match the citations shown on screen
+
+## Design decisions
+
+- **Sidebar History tab:** removed, together with `ConversationHistory.tsx` (in-scope item 10). The sidebar now shows only the document list, under a "Documents (n)" header. The exchange count lives in the conversation header instead.
+- **Layout:** the conversation fills the right panel above the question input. A selected document opens in a strip above the conversation (max 40% height, with a Close button), so following a citation never hides the conversation.
+- **Pending-turn reconciliation:** after `qa.ask` resolves, the renderer reloads `conversation.get()` and then sets the history and clears the pending turn in the same synchronous block, so no render shows the question twice. If the reload fails, it appends `{question, response}` locally instead. A `useRef` guard blocks double submits even before React state updates; the Ask button uses `aria-disabled` rather than `disabled`, so it keeps focus.
+- **Focus styles:** one `:focus-visible` rule in `index.html`, because inline styles cannot express pseudo-classes. The input's inline `outline: none` was removed.
+- **Display helpers:** `components/conversation-format.ts` (`formatTimestamp`, `describeConfidence`, `describeAskError`) is display-only and unit-tested by `conversation-format.test.ts`: `npx vitest run` → 7 passed.
+
+## Known limitations / risks
+
+1. **Keyboard reach.** The conversation comes before the input in DOM order, so a keyboard user reaches the newest citations from the input with **Shift+Tab**. Forward Tab cycles through the header, the documents panel and every earlier citation first.
+2. **Pre-existing, out of scope: status bar.** The status bar shows an empty "Index:" and "Documents:", because `indexing.status` returns the IndexingService's status shape, not `AppStatus`. This is visible in every screenshot and was not introduced by this sprint.
+3. **Pre-existing, out of scope: CSP warning.** Electron's dev-mode "Insecure Content-Security-Policy" `console.warning` appears on load. There are no console errors.
+4. **Mock answer quality.** Answers come from the mock `QaService`. For example, the indexing question matched the "import/document" pattern first, so the answer text is about importing.
+5. **Error detail text.** The error turn shows a "Details:" line with the raw `SyntaxError` text from main. This helps debugging, but it is technical wording for end users.
